n1;}\r\n--></style>\r\n<p>I&#39;ve been thinking of keeping notes as I play the game.&nbsp; Normally the roll of keeping track of the villain turn falls to me, and frankly, it&#39;s easy to forget bits. While I&#39;ve never kicked myself about it, I&#39;d like to more accurately play the game.</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\">For these notes, I think a shorthand of sorts would be useful. What to people think of the following:</p><p>I divide a sheet into two columns and three rows. The columns are for the Villian and Environment. The rows are &quot;beginning of turn&quot;, &quot;During a turn or elsewhen&quot;, and &quot;end of turn&quot;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The notes are abbreviated as follows:</p><p>An up arrow, a number &#39;X&#39;, a &quot;H&quot; or &quot;H+E&quot;, a dash then number &#39;y&#39;: Highest 4 Hero (or hero plus environment) targets take &quot;y&quot; damage</p><p>A down arrow, etc. would denote damage to the lowest HP targets</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Things like a backlash field, additional damage, etc. are noted in the middle:</p><p>A backlash field is sort of like a &quot;K&quot; except the top bit has an outgoing arrow (picture Calvin saying &#39;pa-Ting!&#39;) followed by the amount of damage</p><p>&quot;V+1&quot; = Villain targets do one extra damage</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Can people think of other quick abbreviations needed to make this work? I know that there are counters to help with this, but I&#39;ve not had them work that well.</p><p>Thanks in advance.</p>",
